39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,It appears the data is quite revealing. We have significant disparities in room-by-room energy consumption and a history of payment delays linked to confusion over fluctuating amounts. Clarity seems to be our primary deficiency.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, that's a lot of work! I looked into a template and another house, and it seems like calculating everything by hand takes forever. We really need a way to keep this simple and fast!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems the fluctuations in our bills are quite significant, and the payment delays suggest a lack of clarity. It is concerning that some felt the need to query the amounts before paying.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The fluctuations are indeed stark; the difference between winter and summer is substantial. Furthermore, installing sub-meters would be a significant upfront expense and require ongoing maintenance. We must consider if such a cost is justifiable.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Minato,,I saw that some payments were very late and people were confused. It makes me sad that we had to argue about the money. Can we find a way to stop feeling upset?,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, while sub-meters are expensive, the current ""confusion"" is a cost of its own. If we simply split everything equally, those of us who are mindful of our usage effectively subsidize the heavy users.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I get that, but if the system is too complicated, someone is going to spend their whole evening doing math! We need a balance between being fair and not making it a huge chore.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I understand your point about subsidies. However, we should be careful not to let assumptions create tension. If we can find a method that is both transparent and simple, we can resolve these frustrations.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, I understand your desire for precision, but we must weigh the cost of sub-meters against the actual savings. A high upfront fee and annual maintenance could be more burdensome than the current fluctuations.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, @Victoria, maybe we don't need expensive machines to be fair. I'm worried that if we only talk about numbers, we'll forget that people's feelings were hurt. Can we pick a way that makes everyone feel trusted?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minato, trust is built on transparency, not ambiguity. If we ignore the fact that some use four times more energy than others, we aren't being kind; we are simply ignoring a source of future resentment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I totally get that! But transparency shouldn't mean a nightmare of paperwork. If the ""fair"" way takes hours of work every month, someone's going to get burnt out. Can we find a shortcut?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, perhaps a standardized template could be the shortcut we need. If we can automate the calculations, we can achieve the transparency Benjamin wants without the burden of manual labor.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, a template may simplify the process, but it does not solve the issue of extreme seasonal volatility. We need a system that prevents the winter bills from becoming an unexpected financial burden for any of us.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I agree that big bills are scary. But I'm more scared of us being mean to each other. If we use a template, can we also make a rule to be extra kind when we ask for money?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, a fixed monthly average could mitigate seasonal shocks. However, we must decide if we are splitting the total cost equally or based on usage. I would prefer the latter to avoid silent resentment.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I'm with you on avoiding resentment, but please remember that someone has to actually do the work! If we go with usage, let's make sure it's a system that doesn't eat up our free time.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, @Mio, I believe a fixed monthly average combined with a simple, automated template would address both the seasonal shocks and the labor. This would provide the stability and clarity needed to stop the cycle of queries and delays.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, a fixed average would certainly provide the stability I am looking for. However, we must ensure the total is based on actual annual data so we aren't underpaying and facing a massive deficit later.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I think @Jonathan's idea sounds very peaceful. If we have a fixed amount and a template, maybe we won't have to argue or feel sad about the money anymore. I hope we can all agree.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
