64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option C is the only choice that addresses the actual disparity in usage. While Option B offers stability, it still allows the mindful to subsidize the wasteful. Let us be honest about our habits now.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I really don't like Option C! I saw how long it takes to log readings at another house, and it's a total nightmare. Let's go with Option B; it's way simpler!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, while I value precision, Option C might introduce a new kind of tension through constant monitoring. Option B provides the stability and predictability that can prevent the frustrations we've seen in the payment logs.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, the cost of installing and maintaining meters is too high to justify. Option B is the most rational choice; it provides the financial predictability I need while avoiding an expensive upfront investment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I'm worried that meters might make us feel like we're being watched. Option B sounds much gentler. If we all know the price, we can just be happy and not worry about the numbers.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, @Jonathan, @Victoria, @Minato, your desire for simplicity is noted. However, ""gentle"" systems often mask unfairness. If we choose Option B, are we agreeing that it is acceptable for some to pay for others' luxury?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Jonathan"",""Victoria"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, it's not about luxury, it's about our sanity! If we spend hours every month fighting over pennies or doing math, we'll be way more stressed than if we just pay a bit more. Let's keep it simple!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the ""luxury"" you mention is often a matter of perspective or necessity. I believe the peace of mind gained from a predictable, stable system is more valuable than the pursuit of absolute mathematical precision.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, absolute precision is an illusion if the cost of achieving it exceeds the benefit. Option B allows us to manage our budgets without the stress of sudden spikes or the burden of high installation fees.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I don't want anyone to feel it's unfair, but I think being kind to each other is more important than being perfectly right. Option B feels like it would make us all smile more.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a fascinating paradox that you all find the prospect of fairness more stressful than the prospect of inequality. Very well, if the majority prefers a comfortable illusion over a precise reality, I shall yield.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Mio,,"Yay! I'm so glad we're on the same page, Benjamin! Let's just make sure we keep the year-end settle super quick so it doesn't become a huge project. I'm voting for Option B!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I believe Option B is the most harmonious choice. It resolves the instability of the bills and the confusion of the payments without creating a climate of surveillance. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. Option B provides the necessary financial stability and avoids the prohibitive costs of sub-meters. It is the most sustainable and rational path forward for all of us. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'm happy that we all agree. I want us to be a family that cares about each other more than the bills. I vote for Option B too!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Since the consensus is overwhelming and my appeals for precision have fallen on deaf ears, I shall not be the lone holdout. For the sake of harmony, I vote for Option B.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Mio,,Everything is settled! I'm so happy we could figure this out together without any fighting. Option B it is! Let's make sure we keep it simple and fun!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,It is a relief that we have reached a consensus. May this new arrangement bring us all a sense of stability and peace in our home.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
82,3,4,pass,Jonathan,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
83,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I am glad we have reached a rational agreement. Option B ensures that none of us are blindsided by winter costs, which is the most sustainable way to manage our shared living. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm so glad we could all be kind and agree. I hope we can all be happy and friendly from now on. I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
